# Line-ending policy: LF in the repository AND in the working copy, on every platform.
# Added 2026-07-15 to stop CRLF churn showing up as phantom diffs on Windows; eol=lf added
# 2026-07-29 because text=auto alone still let core.autocrlf ask for CRLF working copies,
# producing a wall of "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings on every Windows commit that
# touched LF files. Modern Windows tooling (VS Code, IntelliJ, PowerShell 5+) is fine with
# LF working copies; cmd.exe scripts keep their CRLF override below.
#
# After pulling this change, normalize once:  git add --renormalize .  and commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch scripts must stay CRLF or cmd.exe mangles multi-line parsing.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts must stay LF or the shebang line breaks.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary formats — never normalize.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.jar binary
*.zip binary
